# Banking Database Analysis (SQL Server)

## Project Overview
This project focuses on designing and analyzing a relational banking database using SQL Server. It explores customer information, bank accounts, transactions, branches, cards, and loan repayment activities.

## Database Tables
- Customers
- Accounts
- Branches
- Cards
- Transactions
- Loans
- Loan_Payments

## Tools & Technologies
- SQL Server
- SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)
- SQL

## Key SQL Concepts
- CREATE TABLE and INSERT
- Primary Keys and Foreign Keys
- JOINs
- Subqueries
- Common Table Expressions (CTEs)
- Window Functions
- Aggregate Functions

## Analysis Objectives
- Analyze customer account information.
- Examine banking transactions.
- Analyze loan details and repayment trends.
- Understand customer activity across branches.

## Project File
- Banking_Database_Analysis.sql

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates relational database development and SQL querying skills for analyzing banking operations and extracting meaningful insights.
